const queue = /* result of the function call below */;
```

In the assistant’s environment, the tool call would look like this:

```commentary
functions.B({
  t: "5",   // concurrency level (as a string)
  // e and n are optional – we’re not adding any initial tasks or payload size here
});
```

When the tool executes, it will return an object that behaves like a typical
task queue (with `.add`, `.on`, etc.).  
You can then paste the returned value into the placeholder above (`/* result of the function call below */`) and run the script.

